"program_narrative": "Program SECMGR is an online CICS security subprogram that receives a SECURITY-REQUEST-AREA (PROCEDURE DIVISION USING) and returns to CICS. The request type selects one of three services: 'V' validates the user by obtaining the CICS signed-on user ID and comparing it with SEC-USER-ID; 'A' checks authorization by counting rows in DB2 table AUTHFILE for the user, resource and access type; 'L' writes an audit row (timestamp, user, terminal, transaction, program, access type) into DB2 table AUDITLOG. Each service reports its result in SEC-RESPONSE-CODE: 0 for success, 8 for a business rejection ('User validation failed', 'Access denied') and 12 for a technical failure ('Unable to obtain user credentials', 'Authorization check failed', 'Audit logging failed'), with the text in SEC-ERROR-INFO. Any other request type does nothing. The authorization count is fetched into the group WS-DB2-AREA, whose numeric meaning is ambiguous, and SQLCODE comes from the precompiler SQLCA, which is not defined in the repository copybook.",
